rules_version = '2';

// Deny every client. This is intentional and not a placeholder.
//
// The device never talks to Firestore. It only ever calls the `talk` function,
// authenticated with X-Api-Key, and that function reads and writes history
// through the Admin SDK - which runs with service-account privileges and
// bypasses these rules entirely.
//
// So the only traffic these rules can possibly govern is a web or mobile SDK
// client, and nothing of the sort exists in this project. Leaving a permissive
// rule here would expose every device's conversation history to anyone who
// learned the project ID, and buy nothing in return.
//
// A companion app now DOES exist (the React dashboard under /app), and it still
// does not touch Firestore: it calls the same function over HTTPS with a Firebase
// ID token, and the uid is derived from that token server-side. Keep it that way.
//
// accounts/{uid} in particular holds a TOKEN BALANCE, which is money. If these
// rules are ever loosened per-collection, that one stays denied to clients
// unconditionally - a readable balance is harmless, a writable one is free
// inference for anyone with the project id. Grants and debits happen only in
// functions/index.js (grantTokens / debitTokens) and in a deliberate admin
// script, both of which run with service-account privileges and bypass rules.
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
